  "question": "A body of mass 5 kg is lifted to a height of 10 m. Calculate potential energy.",
  "gold_answer": "# Solved Numerical\n\n---\n\n## Potential Energy Assessment\n\n### Problem\nA body of mass $5 \\text{ kg}$ is lifted vertically to a height of $10 \\text{ m}$. Calculate its gravitational potential energy.\n\n### Given\n* Mass of the body ($m$) = $5 \\text{ kg}$\n* Vertical height ($h$) = $10 \\text{ m}$\n* Acceleration due to gravity ($g$) = $9.8 \\text{ m/s}^2$\n\n### Formula\n$$U = mgh$$\n\n### Substitution\n$$U = 5 \\times 9.8 \\times 10$$\n\n### Calculation\n$$U = 49 \\times 10$$\n\n$$U = 490 \\text{ J}$$\n\n### Final Answer\n**Potential Energy ($U$) = $490 \\text{ J}$**\n\n### Interpretation\nThis indicates that lifting the object stores $490 \\text{ Joules}$ of mechanical energy within the gravity field, which can convert back into kinetic energy if the object is released.",
  "candidate_response": "<thinking>\nThe user wants to calculate potential energy. Let me provide a well-structured, interactive textbook-style response with proper UI blocks, formula cards, and organized sections.\n\nThe formula for potential energy is:\nPE = mgh\n\nWhere:\n- m = 5 kg\n- g = 9.8 m/s² (standard gravity)\n- h = 10 m\n\nPE = 5 × 9.8 × 10 = 490 J\n\nLet me structure this as an interactive textbook with cards, formula cards, solution steps, etc.\n</thinking>\n\n<div style=\"font-family: 'Segoe UI', sans-serif; max-width: 720px; display: flex; flex-direction: column; gap: 16px;\">\n\n<!-- Topic Badge -->\n<div style=\"display: inline-flex; align-items: center; gap: 8px; background: #eff6ff; border: 1px solid #bfdbfe; border-radius: 20px; padding: 6px 14px; width: fit-content;\">\n  <span style=\"font-size: 13px; color: #1d4ed8; font-weight: 600;\">⚡ Work, Energy & Power</span>\n</div>\n\n<!-- Quick Definition Card -->\n<div style=\"background: #f0fdf4; border: 1px solid #86efac; border-radius: 12px; padding: 20px;\">\n  <div style=\"font-size: 11px; font-weight: 700; color: #16a34a; letter-spacing: 1px; text-transform: uppercase; margin-bottom: 8px;\">📖 Quick Definition</div>\n  <div style=\"font-size: 15px; color: #166534; line-height: 1.6;\">\n    <strong>Gravitational Potential Energy</strong> is the energy stored in an object due to its position above the ground. The higher the object, the more energy it holds.\n  </div>\n</div>\n\n<!-- Formula Card -->\n<div style=\"background: #1e1e2e; border-radius: 12px; padding: 24px; color: white;\">\n  <div style=\"font-size: 11px; font-weight: 700; color: #a78bfa; letter-spacing: 1px; text-transform: uppercase; margin-bottom: 16px;\">📐 Core Formula</div>\n  <div style=\"background: #2a2a3e; border-radius: 8px; padding: 20px; text-align: center; font-size: 22px; margin-bottom: 16px;\">\n\n$$PE = m \\times g \\times h$$\n\n  </div>\n  <!-- Variable Table -->\n  <div style=\"display: grid; grid-template-columns: 1fr 1fr 1fr; gap: 8px; margin-top: 12px;\">\n    <div style=\"background: #2a2a3e; border-radius: 8px; padding: 10px; text-align: center;\">\n      <div style=\"font-size: 18px; color: #f472b6;\">m</div>\n      <div style=\"font-size: 11px; color: #94a3b8; margin-top: 4px;\">Mass (kg)</div>\n    </div>\n    <div style=\"background: #2a2a3e; border-radius: 8px; padding: 10px; text-align: center;\">\n      <div style=\"font-size: 18px; color: #34d399;\">g</div>\n      <div style=\"font-size: 11px; color: #94a3b8; margin-top: 4px;\">Gravity (m/s²)</div>\n    </div>\n    <div style=\"background: #2a2a3e; border-radius: 8px; padding: 10px; text-align: center;\">\n      <div style=\"font-size: 18px; color: #60a5fa;\">h</div>\n      <div style=\"font-size: 11px; color: #94a3b8; margin-top: 4px;\">Height (m)</div>\n    </div>\n  </div>\n</div>\n\n<!-- Given Values Card -->\n<div style=\"background: #fefce8; border: 1px solid #fde68a; border-radius: 12px; padding: 20px;\">\n  <div style=\"font-size: 11px; font-weight: 700; color: #92400e; letter-spacing: 1px; text-transform: uppercase; margin-bottom: 12px;\">📋 Given Values</div>\n  <div style=\"display: flex; flex-direction: column; gap: 8px;\">\n    <div style=\"display: flex; align-items: center; gap: 10px;\">\n      <span style=\"background: #fcd34d; color: #78350f; font-weight: 700; padding: 2px 10px; border-radius: 20px; font-size: 13px;\">m</span>\n      <span style=\"color: #78350f; font-size: 15px;\">= <strong>5 kg</strong></span>\n    </div>\n    <div style=\"display: flex; align-items: center; gap: 10px;\">\n      <span style=\"background: #fcd34d; color: #78350f; font-weight: 700; padding: 2px 10px; border-radius: 20px; font-size: 13px;\">g</span>\n      <span style=\"color: #78350f; font-size: 15px;\">= <strong>9.8 m/s²</strong> <span style=\"font-size: 12px; color: #a16207;\">(standard value)</span></span>\n    </div>\n    <div style=\"display: flex; align-items: center; gap: 10px;\">\n      <span style=\"background: #fcd34d; color: #78350f; font-weight: 700; padding: 2px 10px; border-radius: 20px; font-size: 13px;\">h</span>\n      <span style=\"color: #78350f; font-size: 15px;\">= <strong>10 m</strong></span>\n    </div>\n  </div>\n</div>\n\n<!-- Step by Step Solution -->\n<div style=\"background: white; border: 1px solid #e2e8f0; border-radius: 12px; padding: 20px;\">\n  <div style=\"font-size: 11px; font-weight: 700; color: #475569; letter-spacing: 1px; text-transform: uppercase; margin-bottom: 16px;\">🔢 Step-by-Step Solution</div>\n\n  <!-- Step 1 -->\n  <div style=\"display: flex; gap: 14px; margin-bottom: 16px;\">\n    <div style=\"min-width: 28px; height: 28px; background: #6366f1; color: white; border-radius: 50%; display: flex; align-items: center; justify-content: center; font-weight: 700; font-size: 13px;\">1</div>\n    <div>\n      <div style=\"font-weight: 600; color: #1e293b; margin-bottom: 4px;\">Write the formula</div>\n      <div style=\"background: #f8fafc; border-radius: 8px; padding: 10px; font-size: 15px;\">$$PE = m \\times g \\times h$$</div>\n    </div>\n  </div>\n\n  <!-- Step 2 -->\n  <div style=\"display: flex; gap: 14px; margin-bottom: 16px;\">\n    <div style=\"min-width: 28px; height: 28px; background: #6366f1; color: white; border-radius: 50%; display: flex; align-items: center; justify-content: center; font-weight: 700; font-size: 13px;\">2</div>\n    <div>\n      <div style=\"font-weight: 600; color: #1e293b; margin-bottom: 4px;\">Substitute the values</div>\n      <div style=\"background: #f8fafc; border-radius: 8px; padding: 10px; font-size: 15px;\">$$PE = 5 \\times 9.8 \\times 10$$</div>\n    </div>\n  </div>\n\n  <!-- Step 3 -->\n  <div style=\"display: flex; gap: 14px;\">\n    <div style=\"min-width: 28px; height: 28px; background: #6366f1; color: white; border-radius: 50%; display: flex; align-items: center; justify-content: center; font-weight: 700; font-size: 13px;\">3</div>\n    <div>\n      <div style=\"font-weight: 600; color: #1e293b; margin-bottom: 4px;\">Multiply step by step</div>\n      <div style=\"background: #f8fafc; border-radius: 8px; padding: 10px; font-size: 15px;\">$$5 \\times 9.8 = 49 \\quad \\Rightarrow \\quad 49 \\times 10 = 490$$</div>\n    </div>\n  </div>\n</div>\n\n<!-- Final Answer Card -->\n<div style=\"background: linear-gradient(135deg, #6366f1, #8b5cf6); border-radius: 12px; padding: 24px; text-align: center; color: white;\">\n  <div style=\"font-size: 12px; font-weight: 700; letter-spacing: 1.5px; text-transform: uppercase; opacity: 0.8; margin-bottom: 10px;\">✅ Final Answer</div>\n  <div style=\"font-size: 36px; font-weight: 800; margin-bottom: 6px;\">490 J</div>\n  <div style=\"font-size: 14px; opacity: 0.85;\">$$PE = 490 \\text{ Joules}$$</div>\n</div>\n\n<!-- Key Takeaways -->\n<div style=\"background: #f8fafc; border: 1px solid #e2e8f0; border-radius: 12px; padding: 20px;\">\n  <div style=\"font-size: 11px; font-weight: 700; color: #475569; letter-spacing: 1px; text-transform: uppercase; margin-bottom: 12px;\">💡 Key Takeaways</div>\n  <div style=\"display: flex; flex-direction: column; gap: 10px;\">\n    <div style=\"display: flex; gap: 10px; align-items: flex-start;\">\n      <span style=\"color: #6366f1; font-size: 16px;\">▸</span>\n      <span style=\"color: #334155; font-size: 14px; line-height: 1.5;\">Potential energy <strong>increases</strong> with height — double the height, double the energy.</span>\n    </div>\n    <div style=\"display: flex; gap: 10px; align-items: flex-start;\">\n      <span style=\"color: #6366f1; font-size: 16px;\">▸</span>\n      <span style=\"color: #334155; font-size: 14px; line-height: 1.5;\">The SI unit of energy is the <strong>Joule (J)</strong>.</span>\n    </div>\n    <div style=\"display: flex; gap: 10px; align-items: flex-start;\">\n      <span style=\"color: #6366f1; font-size: 16px;\">▸</span>\n      <span style=\"color: #334155; font-size: 14px; line-height: 1.5;\">This stored energy converts to <strong>Kinetic Energy</strong> when the body falls.</span>\n    </div>\n  </div>\n</div>\n\n</div>",
